To @Centril, @moxian, and @rkruppe for commenting on this on Discord.

Extend Rust's pattern matching exhaustiveness checks to cover the integer types: `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`, `usize`, `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `i128`, `isize` and `char`.

[Rendered.](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/2591-exhaustive-integer-pattern-matching.md)

```rust
fn matcher_full(x: u8) {
  match x { // ok
    0 ..= 31 => { /* ... */ }
    32 => { /* ... */ }
    33 ..= 255 => { /* ... */ }
  }
}

fn matcher_incomplete(x: u8) {
  match x { //~ ERROR: non-exhaustive patterns: `32u8..=255u8` not covered
    0 ..= 31 => { /* ... */ }
  }
}
```

This feature has already [been implemented](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/50912) behind the feature flag `exhaustive_integer_patterns`, so this RFC is viewed as a motion to stabilise the feature. See https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/50912#issuecomment-393991509 for the previous motion to (unstably) approve this feature.

### [🖼️ Rendered](https://github.com/Centril/rfcs/blob/rfc/attributes-galore/text/0000-attributes-galore.md)

### 📝 Summary

[proptest]: https://github.com/altsysrq/proptest

Permit attributes to be attached to lifetimes, types, bounds, and constraints as well as associated type equality constraints `Foo<#[attr] Assoc = MyType>`. For example, in a hypothetical version of [proptest] one may write:

```rust
#[proptest]
// #[quickcheck] could also work similarly.
fn addition_commutes(
    // Run this test for (u8, u8), (u16, u16), and (u32, u32);
    // This is interpreted by `#[proptest]`.
    (a, b): #[types(T, u8, u16, u32)] (T, T)
) -> bool {
    a + b == b + a
}

// Accept x: u8 and vec: Vec<{ y: u8 | y > x }>.
// This is then verified by an external tool.
fn refined(x: u8, vec: Vec<#[require = "> x"] u8>) { ... }
```

