This RFC is about adding local loop bindings.

[Rendered](https://github.com/porky11/rfcs/blob/7fea233dc787c0263c4ac7bcdaa488cab4a3b403/text/0000-local-loop-bindings.md)

Here a simple example for the new syntax:

```rust
fn factorial(x: i32) -> i32 {
    loop (result, count) = (1, x) {
        if count == 1 {
            break result;
        }
        (result * count, count - 1)
    }
}
```

TLDR: Allow

```rust
const fn add<T: Add>(a: T, b: T) -> T::Output {
    a + b
}
```

and

```rust
pub struct Foo<T: Trait>(T);
impl<T: ?const Trait> Foo<T> {
    fn new(t: T) -> Self {
        // not calling methods on `t`, so we opt out of requiring
        // `<T as Trait>` to have const methods via `?const`
        Self(t)
    }
}
```

